    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x-3}-2$. Find the gradient of the inverse function at $x=-5$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The gradient does not exist because $-5$ is outside the domain of $f^{-1}$.",
      "worked": "The range of $f$ is $[-2,\\infty)$, so the domain of $f^{-1}$ is $[-2,\\infty)$. Since $-5<-2$, $f^{-1}(-5)$ is undefined. Therefore the gradient does not exist.",
